    {
      "id": "claim_a7c1b9b102d64c2dbe34ead4095b3f1f",
      "statement": "DiskManager::write_data_with_filters uses a three-stage approach: Stage 1 (shared read lock) inspects the inode and detects Seekable 64K fast path or captures state for standard path; Stage 2 (zero filesystem locks) performs CPU-bound filtering/compression/encryption via plan_write_prepared producing a WritePlan with four cases (FullOverwrite, CompressedAppend, Recompress, Raw); Stage 3 (exclusive write lock) verifies inode_gen staleness, uses prepared plan or re-computes, then commits via journal (single WAL transaction) or legacy in-place path, and syncs per durability mode.",
